          deckDescription: 'One standard 52-card deck consisting of four suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs), each with thirteen ranks from ace down to two. No jokers; used for Bastard Brag (three-card hand game) with prials, runs, and flushes.',
          suitDescription: 'Four French suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs). Flushes (three of the same suit) and running flushes (sequence in one suit) are valid hands. Suits do not break ties except within flush and run hands.',
          rankDescription: 'Thirteen ranks per suit: ace high in prials and runs (e.g. A-K-Q), then king down to two. Standard Brag order: best is prial (three of a kind), then run, then flush, then high cards. Ace can be high or low in runs.',
          dealPattern: 'Three cards to each player and three cards to the widow simultaneously.',
          bettingLimits: 'NA',
